#: includes/admin/documentation.php:144
msgid "(no badge)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:145
msgid "Self-registered via the public form and verified by clicking the magic link, or registered before the badge system was introduced (version 0.9.8)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:149
msgid "A volunteer can have multiple badges at the same time (e.g. Manual + Social)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:152
msgid "The Send Announcement page (Shifts → Send Announcement) lets you send a custom email to volunteers. Available recipient options:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:154
msgid "Subscribed only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:154
msgid "Volunteers who opted in to announcements (default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:155
msgid "Every volunteer with an email address, regardless of opt-in status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:156
msgid "Split volunteers by whether they currently have an upcoming shift assigned — useful for nudging people who haven't signed up yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:157
msgid "Only the volunteers assigned to a selected shift or department. A live recipient count is shown once you pick one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:158
msgid "Individual volunteer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:158
msgid "Click \"Email\" on any volunteer row to open the form pre-filled for that person."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:160
msgid "The From name and From email can be overridden per send. Use {first_name} and {last_name} as personalisation placeholders, and {shifts} to list each recipient's own upcoming shifts. HTML formatting is supported — the live preview below the form renders the email as it will appear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:161
msgid "A PDF can optionally be attached — it will be sent with every email in that announcement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:162
msgid "Every sent announcement is recorded in the collapsible Send History table on the same page. The table can be filtered by typing and sorted by clicking column headers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:163
msgid "Offline volunteers (no email address) are excluded from all announcement sending. Volunteers can opt out under their profile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:165
msgid "Reminder & Notification Emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:166
msgid "Volunteers are emailed when they are assigned to or removed from a shift, and again as a reminder a configurable number of days before it starts (Settings → Communication → Reminders — leave the days field empty to switch reminders off). All three messages use a rich-text editor and share placeholders such as {first}, {last}, {title}, {start}, {end}, {desc}, and {days}. Each shift can override the sender through a linked WordPress user and/or a manual organizer name and email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:168
msgid "E-mail Design"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:169
msgid "Settings → Communication → E-mail design styles the shared wrapper around every plugin email: a header color, a header title and subtitle shown next to the site logo, a rich-text footer, and — under advanced — custom CSS applied to all emails. The filters below are for changes that go beyond these options."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:171
msgid "Email Template Customization"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:172
msgid "All plugin emails use a shared HTML wrapper so registration links, assignment confirmations, cancellations, and announcements have a consistent look."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:173
msgid "Integrators can customize or fully replace this wrapper in theme code or a small companion plugin using WordPress filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:175
msgid "Adjust template variables such as heading, preheader, site name, or footer text before the final HTML is generated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:176
msgid "Modify only the inner email body HTML while keeping the default wrapper."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:177
msgid "Replace the complete final HTML output if you need a fully custom branded layout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:179
msgid "Example: add this in your theme’s functions.php or a small custom plugin to change the footer text of all EventAdmin emails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:184
msgid "Use a custom plugin instead of editing EventAdmin directly if you want your changes to survive plugin updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:186
msgid "Automatic Cleanup of Unverified Accounts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:187
msgid "A daily background job automatically deletes volunteer accounts that were registered via the public form but whose magic login link expired without ever being clicked. Accounts are only deleted if they have no shift assignments and are not marked as manually added."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:188
msgid "A log of automatically deleted accounts (up to the last 100) is shown at the bottom of the Volunteers page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:190
msgid "Public \"Open Positions\" Overview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:191
msgid "The [eventadmin_open_positions] shortcode shows visitors who are not logged in where volunteers are still needed, grouped by department. Only departments with unfilled slots in upcoming shifts are listed. Put it on a public recruitment page, next to the [eventadmin_register] form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:194
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:200
msgid "\"summary\" (default): one line per department with its open-slot count. \"list\": every open shift, grouped under its department."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:204
msgid "Comma-separated department slugs to limit the output to. Default: all visible departments."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:208
msgid "\"0\" hides the \"We still need volunteers in:\" intro line (summary style only)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:212
msgid "\"1\" also includes shifts whose slots are already filled (list style only)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:216
msgid "\"0\" also includes shifts that have already ended. Default: past shifts are hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:221
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:223
msgid "Do volunteers need an account?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:224
msgid "Yes, they must be logged in to view and join shifts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:226
msgid "How can I assign volunteers manually?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:227
msgid "In the admin dashboard under “Volunteer Overview” for each shift via form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:229
msgid "What happens when shifts are full?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:230
msgid "By default, full shifts are hidden on the volunteer page. You can optionally show them in a separate read-only section by enabling \"Show full shifts to volunteers\" under Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:232
msgid "What is the minimum volunteers field for?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:233
msgid "You can set a minimum number of volunteers per shift. The admin dashboard will highlight shifts that have not reached the minimum with an understaffing warning. This is informational only – no signup rules are enforced based on the minimum."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:235
msgid "Can visitors see where help is needed before registering?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:236
msgid "Yes. Put the [eventadmin_open_positions] shortcode on any public page. It lists every department that still has unfilled slots, needs no login, and by default shows a compact summary — add style=\"list\" for the individual open shifts."
msgstr ""

